/F1 10 Tf (7. Agent design) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F1 10 Tf (LangGraph defines a sequential StateGraph; each node reads the same evolving state) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  dictionary and returns its output fields. It is not a set of autonomous LLM agents) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  chatting with one another. Node roles are:) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 10 Tf (1. Property classification agent: combines supplied fields with deterministic extraction) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  from the description, canonicalizes neighborhood aliases, and validates features.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (2. Comparable retrieval agent: queries the hybrid retriever and returns comparable) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  records plus filter/fallback metadata.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (3. Valuation agent: predicts with the selected regression model and generates SHAP) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  impacts \(or the explicit feature-importance fallback\); if prediction is unavailable,) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  uses a comparable-sale median.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (4. Risk/explainability agent: calculates confidence and uncertainty from completeness,) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  similarity, comparable price spread, and fallback flags, then identifies safeguards.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (5. Decision/insight agent: assembles the user-facing valuation, evidence, impacts, and) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  caveats.) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 10 Tf (Communication is through typed shared state keys \(item, features, comparables,) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  retrieval, valuation, risk, result\) in a fixed edge order. The graph is invoked by the) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  valuation service. If LangGraph cannot initialize, the service calls the same stages) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  sequentially as a deterministic fallback. Claude is a separate post-valuation judge;) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  it is not one of these valuation graph nodes and cannot edit the estimate.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F1 10 Tf (8. Runtime data flow) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F1 10 Tf (1. A user enters a description and any known features in the frontend.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (2. FastAPI validates input bounds and rejects instruction-like query content.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (3. The workflow extracts structured facts, then retrieves comparable properties with) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  filters, semantic search, BM25, and RRF.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (4. The prediction stage uses the trained model. If unavailable, a documented comparable-) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  based fallback may be used.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (5. Risk and explanation stages produce uncertainty, safeguards, evidence, and feature) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  impacts.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (6. The response is returned to the frontend and may be saved in SQLite.) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (7. Optional LLM-as-Judge and DeepEval evaluations run separately and cannot change) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf (  price, range, or confidence.) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 10 Tf (See architecture diagram and API reference.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F1 10 Tf (9. Data and artifacts) Tj
T*
T*
T*
